# economy-online: branch coverage

Every room-level and UI branch that `economy-online` added or changed, one row each: where it is, the branch in one line, and the test that fails when the branch is deleted. It covers the hold grace (`inputGate.ts` and the room's hold reads), the supply crates (`supply.ts` and the room), the dockside shop and the tonic (`shop.ts`, the room, the simulation's step), the rumor changes carried from `intel-online` (`intel.ts`, the room), and the browser (`apps/web/src/shop.ts`, `pageKeys.ts`, `markers.ts`, `matchView.ts`, `seaScene.ts`, `main.ts`).

Each `tested` row was checked by deleting (or neutralising) the branch on a scratch copy of the tree outside the repository, with its own `node_modules/@pirate-sea-race` links, and running the suite named for it: the unit tests (`apps/server/src/inputGate.test.ts`, `shop.test.ts`, `supply.test.ts`, `intel.test.ts`, `packages/simulation/src/simulation.test.ts`, `apps/web/src/shop.test.ts` and `journal.test.ts`), the integration files (`tests/integration/holds.test.ts`, `economy.test.ts`, `intel.test.ts`, `claim.test.ts`), three copies in parallel, and the browser spec `tests/e2e/shop.spec.ts` for what only the page does, one deletion at a time. The same sources with no deletion passed every one of those suites first. The row names the tests that failed (the first two, and how many more); the deletion id says what was deleted (`mutations.py` in the worker's scratch directory). None of those edits is committed.

Rows marked `equivalent` are kept, and deleting them changes nothing a player or a test can observe, for the reason given. Branches removed while building the table: `stepCrates` no longer skips ships held for a duel or a respawn (a held ship does not move, so it touches nothing it had not already touched), and the crate spacing became a parameter so its test can make it bind. No row is `unreachable` or `untested`.

